\f1\b0 \
- downloaded EM-DAT public table with registered academic access\
- dropped technological disasters, different insurance product and worse reporting than 	natural.\
- kept year 2000 and above only, years before that are too sparsely \
-only using adjusted damage and insured costs, but keeping historical values as a reference\
\
- \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Downloaded World Development Indicators via databank.worldbank.org, all countries\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \
\
\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
-used GDP per capita, PPP (constant 2021 international $) series NY.GDP.PCAP.PP.KD. its constant rather than current dollars so that values are comparable across years\
-also used domestic credit to private sector % of GDP, population total, and urban population % ot total\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \
-downloaded worldwide governance indicators (rule of law estimate and government effectiveness estimate), post 2025 methodology revision vintage, used the same file throughout the whole project, from the databank of the world bank.\
- removed disasters that were in 2026 as they lacked CPI details so they were not adjusted\
- removed disasters taking place in remote or small areas, such as canary islands, cook 	islands, Wallis and Futuna islands, as the world bank didn't have any data on their gdp or other 	categories.\
- when there isn't a value the world bank uses .. so replaced with a blank cell to make it not read as text before joining.\

