\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Sample> drop_blanks is the baseline dataset. Rows with total damage of zero or missing are excluded, since the log of zero is undefined. Sample restrictions already applied: natural hazards only, 2000 onwards, events with an inflation-adjusted damage figure, and events with World Bank data available for the country-year.\
Outcome> uncovered \'97 share of total damage not covered by insurance, computed as 1 \uc0\u8722  (insured damage adjusted \'f7 total damage adjusted). Bounded 0 to 1.\
Explanatory variables\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 log_gdp \'97 natural log of GDP per capita, PPP, constant 2021 international $. Logged so equal proportional income differences count equally.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 credit_gdp \'97 domestic credit to private sector, % of GDP. Proxy for financial system depth.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 rule_of_law \'97 WGI Rule of Law estimate. Proxy for institutional quality and contract enforcement.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 log_damage \'97 natural log of total damage adjusted. Controls for event size.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Fixed effects> Hazard-type dummies and year dummies. Hazard because floods, storms and earthquakes are insured through different products in different markets; year to absorb global trends and shocks.\
Standard errors> Clustered by country (iso3). Repeated disasters within a country are not independent observations.\
Baseline estimation> OLS. A fractional logit (GLM, binomial family, same clustering) is run alongside, since the outcome is bounded and OLS ignores that. The two are compared on signs and significance, not on raw coefficient sizes.\
Stacking sequence. The three explanations are adjudicated by running the model three times with growing variable lists, holding hazard and year dummies constant throughout:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 log_gdp alone\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 log_gdp + credit_gdp\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 log_gdp + credit_gdp + rule_of_law\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 The quantity of interest is what happens to the log_gdp coefficient at each step. If it holds, income does independent predictive work. If it collapses toward zero, income was proxying for whatever was just added. Both outcomes are reported.\
Robustness checks, declared in advance, in priority order.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}1 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Re-run the baseline on all three datasets, drop_blanks, blanks_zero, both_present, and report headline coefficients side by side.\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Variance inflation factors for the four numeric explanatory variables; substitute govt_eff for rule_of_law in the baseline.\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}3 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Sample splits: above/below the median of log_gdp; by hazard type; before/after 2010.\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}4 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Confirm no conclusion rests on within-country change between adjacent events; keep all language cross-sectional.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Interpretation rules. Every coefficient is translated into a plain-English sentence before appearing in any document. Conclusions use "falls with" or "is associated with", never "causes". The write-up states that these are conditional correlations, not causal estimates.\
Note on the blanks, EM-DAT records no zero values for insured damage, so a blank cannot be distinguished from a true absence of coverage. drop_blanks may therefore drop uninsured events disproportionately, biasing measured coverage upward. drop_blanks and blanks_zero are treated as bounds rather than main-analysis-and-robustness-check.\
Any change to this specification after results are seen will be logged separately, with the reason and the date.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

